.TH AWCCD 1 "October 2026" "AWCC Linux 0.3.0" "System Daemon Commands"
.SH NAME
awccd \- Universal Autonomous Thermal & Hardware Safety Governor Daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B awccd
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B awccd
is the background autonomous thermal management daemon for the AWCC Linux ecosystem.
It executes closed-loop temperature monitoring across CPU, GPU, VRM, and memory SODIMMs,
applying piecewise-linear fan curves with anti-hunt hysteresis damping when in custom mode.
.PP
On termination (SIGTERM, SIGINT, SIGHUP) or sensor failure,
.B awccd
automatically executes emergency fail-safe fan release back to the BIOS/firmware control curve
to guarantee physical hardware protection.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-sysfs\-root <\fIPATH\fR>
Specify alternative sysfs root directory for mock testing and hardware simulation.
.TP
.B \-\-once
Run a single evaluation cycle and exit immediately.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display help documentation and exit.
.SH SYSTEMD INTEGRATION
The daemon is typically managed by systemd as
.BR awccd.service :
.IP
.B sudo systemctl enable --now awccd.service
.SH SECURITY BOUNDARY
.B awccd
runs with standard root privileges to adjust sysfs hardware nodes without requiring world-writable permissions.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR awccctl (1),
.BR awcc-mode (1),
.BR awcc-lux-dashboard (1)
